# Backward Agent

> Build the finished file first, then walk backward to the last act that would make that file real, then run forward.

## Purpose
Make an agent by naming the done picture before any tools or prompts. The original program lives at fitzyracing1/backward-agent. This page only explains that program in everyday words.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Write one sentence of the world after success and name the file path.
2. Write a test that is true only when that file is good enough.
3. Name the last write or run that would pass the test.
4. List the smallest facts that last write needs.
5. Gather those facts.
6. Turn a short user line into the done picture.
7. Run forward: intake, gather, last act, test.

## Key ideas
- Done picture (the finished world in one sentence)
- Terminal test (a yes-or-no check on a real file)
- Last act (the one write that should finish the job)
- Preconditions (facts you can see before that write)

## The actual code
```
# files in source repo fitzyracing1/backward-agent
SKILL.md
scripts/backward_agent.py
proof/LAYERS.md
proof/LAYERS.json
proof/RESULT.md
index.html

intake -> done picture -> gather -> check preconditions -> last act -> terminal test
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. SKILL.md → “the written rules for last-to-first building”
2. scripts/backward_agent.py → “the program that runs those rules”
3. proof/LAYERS.md → “the six layers written down for one goal”
4. proof/RESULT.md → “proof the test passed”
5. intake -> … -> terminal test → “run order is forward even though the build order was backward”

## Decisions the program makes
- If the test fails → treat the failure as a new done picture one layer back and repeat once
- If the user names no domain → write RESULT.md
- If tools are listed before the test → that is the wrong order; stop and write the test first

## What a person would notice
A readable page that says what the agent is for without asking the reader to open Python first.

## Current status
Barrage clone of a working source repo. Source is not copied file-for-file; the tree is named and explained.

## Next possible steps
Open the source repo and run scripts/backward_agent.py with one goal.
